    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0251" n="167" xml:id="pg167"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr. Beaupré.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1903-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21,
                                1903</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At the instance of the Hon. John T. Morgan,
                    I have to request that you will forward two copies of the proclamation of Acting
                    President Marroquin, calling the session of Congress to consider the canal
                    treaty, and two copies of the law under which the proclamation was issued.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
